course: dictionary
lesson: 13882
title: One word, many meanings: knitted
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Knitted comes from the verb knit, which means to loop wool or yarn together with needles or a machine. When knitted describes something, it tells you how that thing was made: «She wore a knitted scarf in the snow.» The clue is scarf. A scarf is made of wool, so knitted means made by knitting.
explain: Knitted is also the past form of knit, so it tells you that the knitting happened earlier: «Grandma knitted me a hat last winter.» Knit is the present form, and knitted is the one you use when the job is already finished.
explain: Some meanings are not about wool at all. «Dad knitted his brows when he read the letter.» Knitted brows means eyebrows pulled together in worry or thought. The clue is that he read a letter, so he was probably worried. A broken bone can knit too: «The broken arm had knitted well.» Here it means joined and healed.
explain: Close-knit means closely joined, like «a close-knit family». Use the words around knitted to decide which meaning fits: wool, the past, worry, healing or closeness. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Knit means to make cloth by looping wool or yarn together with needles or a machine.
fact: «Knitted» means made by knitting, or it is the past form of knit.
fact: «Knitted brows» means eyebrows pulled together in worry or thought.
fact: A broken bone that has knitted has joined and healed.
fact: «Close-knit» means closely joined, like a close-knit family.
exercise: «She wore a knitted scarf in the snow.» What is knitted here? | Lost in the snow | *Made by looping wool with needles | Pulled together in worry | Healed after a break
exercise: «Grandma knitted me a hat last winter.» Which tense is knitted in this sentence? | Future, it will happen later | *Past, it happened earlier | Present, it is happening now
exercise: «Dad knitted his brows when he read the letter.» What does knitted brows mean? | Eyebrows that have healed | Eyebrows lifted up in surprise | *Eyebrows pulled together in worry or thought | Eyebrows covered with wool
test: «The broken arm had knitted well.» What does knitted mean here? | Very cold | Looped with wool | Dropped on the floor | *Joined and healed
test: «They are a close-knit team who always help each other.» What does close-knit mean? | *Closely joined and supportive | Loud and noisy | Made of wool | Far apart
exam: Which meaning of knitted fits best in «Her knitted gloves kept her hands warm»? | Pulled together in worry | Closely joined | *Made by looping wool with needles | Joined and healed
